From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_L1639_PARK_WAIT, no batch-wide join after the fence action finished (fix to 0986; port of Lichii PR #1639 by DuskDarf1; off unless set)

Upstream: zortos293/Lichii PR #1639 by DuskDarf1. Their scoped action joins "a callback already
running under the syncpoint manager's action lock": upstream runs actions under that lock, so a
deregister joins only its own action. Our SyncpointManager runs due actions outside the guard and a
deregister that misses the list waits until running_actions (one count for all syncpoints) is 0.

Defect in 0986 (read in source, not measured): after a normal wake the action has already left the
list, so leaving the wait waited for the rest of the fence's due batch on the GPU thread, with the
composite of that frame among it (gpu.cpp registers renderer->Composite on the same fence; ours sits
before it in the list), plus any batch on any other syncpoint. That is a host-thread block on guest
core 3 for the composite's length after every present, which 0986 did not have in mind.

Fix: the action's last step sets a per-session flag. When it is set the waiter skips the deregister
(the action is off the list and touches nothing of the session any more). Otherwise (timeout, power
off, fence seen reached before its action ran) it deregisters as before, counted as "deregistered
before their action finished" in the 600-wait line. Unset: nothing changes (code only runs parked).
nx2_gsv.h is not a translation id input: KEEPS THE STORE.

---
diff --git a/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h b/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h
index 8441e0a196..3984fe5e6c 100644
--- a/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h
+++ b/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h
@@ -1909,7 +1909,18 @@ public:
           handle{syncpoints.RegisterGuestAction(id, value, std::forward<Callback>(callback))} {}
 
     ~Nx2ScopedGuestFenceAction() {
-        syncpoints.DeregisterGuestAction(id, handle);
+        if (!finished) {
+            syncpoints.DeregisterGuestAction(id, handle);
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// 0987: the action ran to its end (its last step marks it), so it is off the manager's list
+    /// and touches nothing of the waiter's any more. Then the destructor skips the deregister:
+    /// in our tree a deregister that misses the list waits until no due action runs anywhere
+    /// (running_actions is one count for all syncpoints), which after a normal wake meant waiting
+    /// for the rest of the fence's batch, the composite (renderer->Composite) among it.
+    void MarkFinished() {
+        finished = true;
     }
 
     Nx2ScopedGuestFenceAction(const Nx2ScopedGuestFenceAction&) = delete;
@@ -1919,6 +1930,7 @@ private:
     Tegra::Host1x::SyncpointManager& syncpoints;
     const u32 id;
     const Tegra::Host1x::SyncpointManager::ActionHandle handle;
+    bool finished{};
 };
 
 // Placeholder for the Switch 2 display session (nn::vi2::sdk), handed out by gsv 305. Reply
@@ -2877,15 +2889,18 @@ private:
         auto& syncpoints = system.Host1x().GetSyncpointManager();
         m_park_event->Clear(kernel);
         m_park_signal_ns.store(0, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+        m_park_fired.store(false, std::memory_order_relaxed);
         // Runs on the GPU thread as it reaches the fence, or inline here if it already did.
+        // Its last step marks it finished (0987): nothing of this session is touched after it.
         m_park_action.emplace(syncpoints, fence_id, fence_value,
                               [event = m_park_event, kernel_ptr = &kernel,
-                               signal_ns = &m_park_signal_ns] {
+                               signal_ns = &m_park_signal_ns, fired = &m_park_fired] {
                                   signal_ns->store(std::chrono::steady_clock::now()
                                                        .time_since_epoch()
                                                        .count(),
                                                    std::memory_order_relaxed);
                                   event->Signal(*kernel_ptr);
+                                  fired->store(true, std::memory_order_release);
                               });
         Kernel::KSynchronizationObject* object = &m_park_event->GetReadableEvent();
         while (!syncpoints.IsReadyGuest(fence_id, fence_value) && system.IsPoweredOn() &&
@@ -2903,7 +2918,14 @@ private:
                 break;
             }
         }
-        // Join an action still signalling before the next wait clears the event.
+        // An action that finished needs no deregister (0987). Otherwise (timeout, power off, or
+        // the fence seen reached before its action ran) remove it, or join it if it is running,
+        // before the next wait clears the event; that join can wait for the fence's whole batch.
+        if (m_park_fired.load(std::memory_order_acquire)) {
+            m_park_action->MarkFinished();
+        } else {
+            ++m_park.deregistered;
+        }
         m_park_action.reset();
         const auto end = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
         const s64 signalled = m_park_signal_ns.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
@@ -2932,13 +2954,13 @@ private:
         LOG_INFO(Service,
                  "EDEN_UP_L1639_PARK_WAIT: last {} frame waits (to present #{}): {} parked "
                  "(avg {} us, {} kernel waits, {} 50-ms timeouts, {} ended by termination), "
-                 "signal-to-run avg {} us max {} us over {}; host wait kept: {} not on a guest "
-                 "thread, {} without an event",
+                 "signal-to-run avg {} us max {} us over {}, {} deregistered before their action "
+                 "finished; host wait kept: {} not on a guest thread, {} without an event",
                  m_park.waits, m_presents, m_park.parked,
                  m_park.parked != 0 ? m_park.parked_us / m_park.parked : 0, m_park.kernel_waits,
                  m_park.timeouts, m_park.terminated,
                  m_park.woken != 0 ? m_park.wake_us / m_park.woken : 0, m_park.wake_max_us,
-                 m_park.woken, m_park.host_thread, m_park.no_event);
+                 m_park.woken, m_park.deregistered, m_park.host_thread, m_park.no_event);
         const bool first_logged = m_park.first_logged;
         m_park = {};
         m_park.first_logged = first_logged;
@@ -2954,6 +2976,7 @@ private:
         u64 woken{};
         u64 wake_us{};
         u64 wake_max_us{};
+        u64 deregistered{};
         u64 host_thread{};
         u64 no_event{};
         bool first_logged{};
@@ -2962,6 +2985,7 @@ private:
     Kernel::KEvent* m_park_event{};
     bool m_park_event_tried{};
     std::atomic<s64> m_park_signal_ns{0};
+    std::atomic<bool> m_park_fired{false};
     std::optional<Nx2ScopedGuestFenceAction> m_park_action;
 
     /// Waits until the fence is reached. With `unless_gpu_waits`, gives up after a few ms once a
